{"step_index":43,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-27T03:34:47Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-27T09:04:47+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-08-27T09:04:47+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/mcp/vidiq/vidiq_generate_titles.json`\nTotal Lines: 1\nTotal Bytes: 3068\nShowing lines 1 to 1\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: {\"name\":\"vidiq_generate_titles\",\"description\":\"Generate scored YouTube title suggestions.\\n\\nProvide at least one of `videoId`, `title`, or `description`. With\\nonly `videoId`, the current title/description are fetched from YouTube.\\n\\nCost: 5 credit(s) per call.\",\"parameters\":{\"$schema\":\"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\"properties\":{\"analysisSummary\":{\"description\":\"Pre-computed analysis summary. When provided, upstream skips its own analysis pass (transcript/frames → Gemini) and uses this directly. Useful when chaining after a tool that already produced video understanding. Capped at 4000 chars.\",\"maxLength\":4000,\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"},\"competitorTitles\":{\"description\":\"Seed titles for the competitive context block. When provided, upstream skips its Outliers lookup and uses these directly — useful for deterministic output or when the caller already has a curated competitor set. Capped at 20 entries x 200 chars; duplicates removed.\",\"items\":{\"maxLength\":200,\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"},\"maxItems\":20,\"type\":\"array\"},\"description\":{\"description\":\"Current video description. When omitted but videoId is provided, fetched from yt-proxy. Caller-supplied value takes precedence.\",\"maxLength\":5000,\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"},\"language\":{\"description\":\"Target language for generated titles and the analysis pass (e.g. 'en', 'pt-BR'). Defaults to English when omitted.\",\"pattern\":\"^[a-z]{2,3}(?:-[a-z]{2,4})?$\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"numTitles\":{\"description\":\"How many title candidates to generate (default: 3)\",\"maximum\":10,\"minimum\":1,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"previousTitles\":{\"description\":\"Recent titles from the same channel. Used by upstream to reduce repetition and improve novelty. Capped at 20 entries x 200 chars; duplicates removed.\",\"items\":{\"maxLength\":200,\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"},\"maxItems\":20,\"type\":\"array\"},\"regionCode\":{\"description\":\"2-letter ISO country code (e.g. 'US', 'BR'). Normalized to uppercase. Used by upstream when fetching competitive context.\",\"pattern\":\"^[a-z]{2}$\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"scoreThreshold\":{\"description\":\"Return only suggestions with score \\u003e= threshold. Thresholds above 70 on long-form videos may legitimately yield no results, and the filter applies before the numTitles top-K slice (so the response may contain fewer items than numTitles).\",\"maximum\":80,\"minimum\":1,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"title\":{\"description\":\"Current/working video title. When omitted but videoId is provided, fetched from yt-proxy. Caller-supplied value takes precedence.\",\"maxLength\":500,\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"},\"type\":{\"description\":\"Video format hint. Affects the generation prompt and scoring rubric. When omitted, upstream infers from duration and otherwise treats the video as long-form.\",\"enum\":[\"long\",\"short\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"videoId\":{\"description\":\"YouTube video ID (e.g. 'dQw4w9WgXcQ'). When provided, the tool fetches the current title/description from yt-proxy to ground generation. Optional when title and/or description are supplied directly.\",\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"}},\"type\":\"object\"}}\nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
