{"step_index":51,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-27T03:34:56Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-27T09:04:56+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-08-27T09:04:56+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/mcp/vidiq/vidiq_ig_accounts_from_outliers.json`\nTotal Lines: 1\nTotal Bytes: 1464\nShowing lines 1 to 1\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: {\"name\":\"vidiq_ig_accounts_from_outliers\",\"description\":\"Find Instagram creator/account candidates from existing outlier reel discovery.\\n\\nUse this when the user asks for Instagram accounts, creators, competitors, influencers, partners, or examples to study. The service groups outlier reels into accounts and verifies candidates against profile and recent content.\\n\\nHow to call:\\n- `niche`: one-line content/account niche. Keep it about the creator's content, not audience demographics.\\n- `audienceQuery`: required audience context in this format: `Culture/Region: ...; Global: \\u003ctrue|false\\u003e; Demographics: ...;`\\n  Derive it from the user's stated target audience or profile/recent reels, not from handle alone. If audience is vague, ask before searching.\\n- Use optional `followersMin` / `followersMax` when account size matters.\\n\\nCost: 10 credit(s) per call.\",\"parameters\":{\"$schema\":\"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\"properties\":{\"audienceQuery\":{\"description\":\"Format: Culture/Region: ...; Global: \\u003ctrue|false\\u003e; Demographics: ...;\",\"maxLength\":500,\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"},\"followersMax\":{\"maximum\":9007199254740991,\"minimum\":0,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"followersMin\":{\"maximum\":9007199254740991,\"minimum\":0,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"niche\":{\"description\":\"One-line description of the Instagram reel/content niche to search for.\",\"maxLength\":500,\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"niche\",\"audienceQuery\"],\"type\":\"object\"}}\nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
{"step_index":52,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-27T03:34:56Z","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\mcp\\vidiq\\vidiq_ig_profile.json","toolAction":"Viewing vidiq_ig_profile.json","toolSummary":"View vidiq_ig_profile.json"}}]}
{"step_index":53,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-27T03:34:58Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-27T09:04:58+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-08-27T09:04:58+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/mcp/vidiq/vidiq_ig_profile.json`\nTotal Lines: 1\nTotal Bytes: 776\nShowing lines 1 to 1\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: {\"name\":\"vidiq_ig_profile\",\"description\":\"Fetch public Instagram profile by handle: bio, follower/following counts, post count, verification, external URL, with the profile picture returned inline.\\n\\nDO NOT USE FOR:\\n- Profile search/discovery — you must already have a handle.\\n- Reels — use `vidiq_ig_profile_reels` (up to 6, popularity-sorted, no pagination).\\n- Stories, Highlights, IGTV, private-account data.\\n- Engagement-rate or growth analytics — snapshot only.\\n\\nCost: 5 credit(s) per call.\",\"parameters\":{\"$schema\":\"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\"properties\":{\"handle\":{\"description\":\"Instagram handle (with or without leading @). 1-30 chars; letters/digits/dot/underscore.\",\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"handle\"],\"type\":\"object\"}}\nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
