{"step_index":63,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-27T03:35:39Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-27T09:05:39+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-08-27T09:05:39+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/mcp/vidiq/vidiq_keyword_research.json`\nTotal Lines: 1\nTotal Bytes: 9330\nShowing lines 1 to 1\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: {\"name\":\"vidiq_keyword_research\",\"description\":\"Research YouTube keywords to find search volume, competition, and related keyword opportunities. This tool returns keyword metrics, NOT videos. To find actual videos, use vidiq_outliers or vidiq_trending_videos instead.\\n\\nThis tool has five modes. Choose with the `mode` parameter based on what the user is asking for:\\n\\n1. `research` (default): full keyword metrics for a seed keyword plus related keyword suggestions. Use for global/topic research (\\\"research minecraft tips\\\", \\\"keyword ideas for cooking\\\"). Returns for each keyword:\\n   - Volume (0-100): How often people search for this keyword on YouTube\\n   - Competition (0-100): How many videos target this keyword\\n   - Overall score (0-100): Combined keyword opportunity score\\n   - Estimated monthly search volume\\n   - View momentum: recent daily views-per-hour data for the seed keyword, when available\\n   - Top markets: the countries where the keyword is most searched, with each country's share of searches\\n   - In-country volume: optionally pass a `country` (ISO 3166-1 alpha-2) to also get each keyword's estimated search volume within that country (the `countryVolume` field)\\n\\n2. `questions`: question-style keyword searches matching a seed keyword, using the same indexed results and metrics as the vidIQ webapp. Requires `keyword`; use `language` to select the question-language index and `limit` to cap results. Set `sort='volume'` (default) for established demand or `sort='trending'` for fastest growth. Results come back in `questions` with question, volume, competition, overall score, estimated monthly searches, and growth.\\n\\n3. `country_search`: the top keywords matching a TOPIC within ONE country and capped at `limit`. Use when the user names BOTH a topic AND a country — e.g. \\\"give me the top 10 minecraft keywords in IN\\\" → mode='country_search', keyword='minecraft', country='IN', limit=10. Requires `country` and `keyword`. Results come back in `relatedKeywords` (each row's `countryVolume` is the in-country volume; global YouTube metrics are null).\\n   - By default (`broad: false`) this is an EXACT/PHRASE match — every returned keyword literally contains the topic words (e.g. 'minecraft' → 'minecraft mods', 'minecraft house').\\n   - Set `broad: true` for a SEMANTIC match: the topic is first expanded into related keywords (the engine behind vidIQ's \\\"Related Keywords\\\" tab). Long-tail candidates preserving multiple meaningful seed terms rank before semantic-only candidates; within each tier, upstream related score then in-country volume determine order. The overlap boost is a lightweight heuristic: simple ASCII suffix matching applies only to ASCII Latin tokens, while other scripts require exact normalized token overlap. Country keyword text may be in any language; the `language` field only affects `questions` and `rising`. Returned keywords need NOT contain the topic words (e.g. 'minecraft' → 'redstone', 'survival mode'). Use this when the user wants a bigger/wider list, says \\\"related\\\"/\\\"similar\\\"/\\\"broaden\\\", or the exact-match list is too small.\\n\\n4. `country_top`: the top keywords overall within ONE country (NO topic filter), ranked by in-country search volume and capped at `limit`. Use when the user names a country but no topic, e.g. \\\"what are the top keywords in Brazil\\\" → mode='country_top', country='BR'. Requires `country`; `keyword` is ignored. Results come back in `relatedKeywords` as above.\\n\\n5. `rising`: keywords gaining search momentum over time, like the vidIQ dashboard's \\\"Rising Keywords\\\" tab. Use when the user asks for rising, trending, or gaining-momentum keywords. Choose the trend window with `period`. Optionally scope to a category with `topic` — this MUST be one of the values in the response's `availableTopics` (call 'rising' with no `topic` first to discover them; passing an unknown topic returns an error listing the valid ones). Omit `topic` for overall trends, in which case `availableTopics` lists every category you can drill into. This returns keyword METRICS with growth, not videos. Results come back in `risingKeywords`, not `relatedKeywords`.\\n\\nCost: 5 credit(s) per call.\",\"parameters\":{\"$schema\":\"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\"properties\":{\"broad\":{\"default\":false,\"description\":\"Only applies to 'country_search' mode. Controls how the topic is matched within the country:\\n- false (default) = EXACT/PHRASE match: returns only keywords whose text actually contains the topic words. E.g. topic 'minecraft' returns 'minecraft', 'minecraft mods', 'minecraft house'; every result literally contains 'minecraft'. Use when the user wants variants of a specific phrase.\\n- true = SEMANTIC/BROAD match: first expands the topic into related keywords (the same engine behind vidIQ's 'Related Keywords' tab). For long-tail seeds, candidates preserving multiple meaningful seed terms rank before semantic-only candidates; within each tier, upstream related score then in-country volume determine order. This is a lightweight overlap heuristic, not language detection: simple ASCII suffix matching applies only to ASCII Latin tokens, while other scripts require exact normalized token overlap. Results need NOT contain the topic words, so a short topic such as 'minecraft' can still return 'redstone', 'survival mode', and 'building ideas'. Use when the user wants a BIGGER / wider list of related ideas, says 'related', 'similar', 'broaden', 'more than just X', or complains the exact-match list is too small.\",\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"country\":{\"description\":\"ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country code (for example 'US', 'IN'). In 'research' mode this is optional and enriches each keyword with its estimated in-country search volume (the `countryVolume` field). REQUIRED for 'country_top' and 'country_search' modes. Not supported in 'rising' mode.\",\"maxLength\":2,\"minLength\":2,\"type\":\"string\"},\"includeRelated\":{\"default\":true,\"description\":\"Include related keyword suggestions ('research' mode only)\",\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"keyword\":{\"description\":\"Seed keyword / topic (for example 'minecraft tips'). Required for 'research', 'questions', and 'country_search'; ignored for 'country_top'; not used in 'rising' (use `topic` to scope rising trends).\",\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"},\"language\":{\"default\":\"en\",\"description\":\"Language for 'questions' or 'rising' mode (case-insensitive). Questions supports any, en, es, pt, ru, sv. Rising supports all, en, ru, es, pt. Defaults to en. This field does not constrain research or country searches.\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"limit\":{\"default\":20,\"description\":\"Maximum number of results to return for 'questions', 'country_top', 'country_search', and 'rising' modes. Ignored in 'research' mode.\",\"maximum\":100,\"minimum\":1,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"mode\":{\"default\":\"research\",\"description\":\"Which kind of keyword research to run. Pick based on the user's question:\\n- 'research' (default): full metrics for a seed keyword plus recent daily views-per-hour momentum and related keyword suggestions (volume, competition, overall score, top markets). Use for global/topic research like 'research minecraft tips' or 'keyword ideas for cooking'. Optionally pass `country` to also enrich every row with its in-country search volume.\\n- 'questions': indexed question-style searches matching a seed keyword, with volume, competition, opportunity, estimated searches, and growth. Use `sort: 'volume'` for established demand or `sort: 'trending'` for fastest growth. Requires `keyword`; `language` controls the question-language index.\\n- 'country_search': the top keywords matching a topic WITHIN one country. By default, exact/phrase matches are ranked by in-country volume. With `broad: true`, long-tail matches preserving meaningful seed terms rank before semantic-only discoveries; within each tier, upstream related score and in-country volume determine order. Requires `country` and `keyword`.\\n- 'country_top': the top keywords overall within one country, ranked by in-country search volume, with NO topic filter. Use when the user names a country but no topic, e.g. 'what are the top keywords in Brazil'. Requires `country`; `keyword` is ignored.\\n- 'rising': keywords gaining search momentum globally over a day, week, or month. Optionally scope to a category via `topic` (a value from `availableTopics`); omit `topic` for overall trends plus the discoverable topic list. Results include growth metrics in `risingKeywords`.\",\"enum\":[\"research\",\"questions\",\"country_top\",\"country_search\",\"rising\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"period\":{\"default\":\"week\",\"description\":\"Trend window for 'rising' mode. Only meaningful in 'rising' mode.\",\"enum\":[\"day\",\"week\",\"month\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"sort\":{\"default\":\"volume\",\"description\":\"Ranking for 'questions' mode: 'volume' (default) ranks by search volume; 'trending' ranks by growth. Ignored in other modes.\",\"enum\":[\"volume\",\"trending\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"topic\":{\"description\":\"Category to scope 'rising' results to (for example 'gaming'). Must be one of the values returned in `availableTopics` — call 'rising' without a `topic` first to discover them. Matching is case-insensitive. Omit for overall (non-topic-scoped) rising trends. Ignored outside 'rising' mode; use `keyword` for the research seed.\",\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"}},\"type\":\"object\"}}\nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
