{"step_index":65,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-27T03:35:41Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-27T09:05:41+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-08-27T09:05:41+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/mcp/vidiq/vidiq_list_competitors.json`\nTotal Lines: 1\nTotal Bytes: 782\nShowing lines 1 to 1\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: {\"name\":\"vidiq_list_competitors\",\"description\":\"List the YouTube channels the user is tracking as competitors of one of their own channels.\\n\\nReturns only channel IDs. To get titles, thumbnails, subscriber counts, etc., pass the IDs to vidiq_get_channels_by_ids.\\n\\nThe youtubeChannelId must be a channel the user has authorized — use vidiq_user_channels to discover them.\\n\\nCost: 0 credit(s) per call.\",\"parameters\":{\"$schema\":\"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\"properties\":{\"youtubeChannelId\":{\"description\":\"YouTube channel ID (e.g. 'UCxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx') of one of the user's own authorized channels. Use vidiq_user_channels first if you don't know which channels the user owns.\",\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"youtubeChannelId\"],\"type\":\"object\"}}\nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
